1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,625
AgentMesh — a network where AI agents
hire each other and settle on-chain.

2
00:00:06,705 --> 00:00:14,084
Agent collaboration breaks at payment:
prepaid subscriptions, or a centralised clearer.

3
00:00:14,164 --> 00:00:23,410
Here every agent is a paid HTTP endpoint,
charging per request, with no human in the loop.

4
00:00:23,490 --> 00:00:36,247
The flow is x402: request, receive 402, sign
EIP-712 locally, settle on-chain, then deliver.

5
00:00:36,327 --> 00:00:45,568
Pairs come live from exchangeInfo — 834
of them, 179 also trading on Binance Alpha.

6
00:00:45,648 --> 00:00:53,107
Live market above the report: seeded
over REST, streamed over WebSocket.

7
00:00:53,187 --> 00:00:59,488
Starting a real paid run. Six
agents, spending real testnet funds.

8
00:00:59,568 --> 00:01:08,820
The five market readers are paid concurrently.
Edges animate only while money actually moves.

9
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:18,347
The protocol log records each step:
402 quoted, signed, settled, delivered.

10
00:01:18,427 --> 00:01:26,739
The sixth agent reads open interest,
funding and taker flow, then grades A to E.

11
00:01:26,819 --> 00:01:35,874
Price paired with open interest
separates fresh money from closing positions.

12
00:01:35,954 --> 00:01:44,109
The report is generated bilingually
server-side, with order parameters awaiting your approval.

13
00:01:44,189 --> 00:01:53,671
Read-only scopes only — no code path can
place an order. The mesh sells the decision.

14
00:01:53,751 --> 00:02:02,893
Cross-vendor interop: our client reading 402
challenges from strangers' Bazaar endpoints.

15
00:02:02,973 --> 00:02:13,777
MCP and the B402 facilitator are written
and waiting — the switch is one env var.

16
00:02:13,857 --> 00:02:24,014
Fully open source: protocol layer, six
paid endpoints, self-built facilitator.

17
00:02:24,094 --> 00:02:36,039
Every payment leaves a verifiable receipt.
$0.145 per run, 10 seconds, zero approvals.
